# GALI-SPINAL TUBE  
**Version 4 – TiC + PTFE, Sphere-Size Scaling**  
**Technical Specification Sheet**

**Date:** 25 April 2026  
**Designer / Concept Origin:** J.Vandamn  
**Status:** Prototype-ready conceptual design (v4.1 with micro-bubble upgrade)

## 1. Overview
The Gali-Spinal Tube is a vertical, sealed magneto-sonic resonance column designed for continuous fluid-dynamic energy transfer and targeted molecular-scale effects. It combines high-performance advanced materials, liquid-metal carrier fluid, size-scaled magnetite resonators, dual-frequency sonic heads, **and two stabilized micro-bubble molecules** to create a driven, high-RPM whipping motion within a Lorentz-force augmented field.

The system produces two distinct output regimes:  
- **Energy Head** – aggressive, high-frequency ionizing output  
- **Molecular Healing Head** – gentler, restorative de-ionizing coherence  

**Intended applications:** advanced materials research, sonochemical processing, plasma-physics studies, and speculative molecular-healing / coherence research.

## 2. Physical Construction
- **Overall Dimensions:** 380 mm height × 65 mm diameter (side-view tube)  
- **Outer Structural Wall:** Titanium Carbide (TiC) – ultra-high hardness (HV 2800–3200), exceptional wear resistance under high RPM and sonic threshold pressure  
- **Inner Lining:** PTFE (polytetrafluoroethylene) – chemically inert, ultra-low friction surface for sphere transit  
- **Sealing:** Double-headed sleeved ferrite at base with pure-iron magnetic return path on one flank  
- **Carrier Fluid:** 40 % DMSO + Galinstan (room-temperature liquid metal alloy) – optional deionized-water variant for lower conductivity tuning  
- **Closed-System Additions:** Two stabilized micro-bubble molecules (see Section 3)

## 3. Active Elements
- **Resonator Spheres:** Highly purified magnetite (Fe₃O₄) spheres  
  - Size-scaled vertically (2 mm base → 8 mm top) for progressive mass increase, stronger centrifugal contribution, and richer MHz harmonic spectrum  
  - **Color code:** black / blue dots  

- **Ionizing / De-ionizing Nodes**  
  - Yellow = ionizing node (sharp-angle, high-frequency)  
  - Green = de-ionizing node (soft-angle, restorative)  

- **Micro-Bubble Molecules (NEW – v4.1)**  
  - **Quantity:** 2 per closed system (one near Energy Head, one near Molecular Healing Head)  
  - **Diameter:** 50–150 µm stabilized micro-bubbles  
  - **Composition:** Trace mercury-vapor / noble-gas core with DMSO-compatible surfactant shell  
  - **Function:** Persistent cavitation nuclei, sonic-threshold seed points, and Lorentz-force coupling enhancers  
  - **Color code:** **Purple** = micro-bubble molecules  

- **Mercurial Reference Points:** Red accents (mercury-channel notes for plasma / hydrogen atmosphere studies)

## 4. Operating Principles
- **Primary Drive:** Lorentz forces generated by external ferrite field interacting with conductive Galinstan carrier under high-RPM centrifugal “whip” motion  
- **Sonic Regime:** Dual MHz resonance bands (energy head: sharp, aggressive high-frequency “song”; healing head: softer green-blue pulsing with restorative coherence glow at sonic crossover)  
- **Fluid Dynamics:** Spheres whip in perpetual-like closed-loop motion through the blue carrier fluid, producing centrifugal force, cavitation nuclei, and harmonic pressure waves  
- **Micro-Bubble Enhancement (NEW):** The two micro-bubbles act as stable, reusable cavitation nuclei. They lower the sonic threshold, amplify MHz harmonic richness, and generate visible micro-plasma flashes at the “snap zone,” directly feeding the DEIMOS Chaos Burst configuration observed at the healing-head crossover.  
- **Energy Transfer:** “Other side” pure-iron magnetic return path completes the circuit; sonic threshold “snap zone” at mid-column creates visible plasma-like coherence effects  

**Note:** System is externally driven (pulsed electromagnetic coil + ultrasonic transducer at base) to maintain stable operation. The micro-bubbles remain suspended and do not escape the sealed PTFE-lined chamber.

## 5. Performance Specifications (Version 4.1)

| Parameter                    | Specification                          | Notes                                      |
|------------------------------|----------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| Operating RPM                | 8 000 – 18 000                         | Sphere-size dependent                      |
| Sonic Frequency              | 1.2 – 4.8 MHz (dual-band)              | Energy head dominant                       |
| Carrier Fluid Temp. Range    | 18 °C – 65 °C                          | Galinstan enables room-temp operation      |
| Magnetic Field Strength      | 0.6 – 1.2 T (ferrite + iron return)   | Lorentz force optimized                    |
| Sphere Mass Scaling Effect   | Progressive 4× mass increase top-to-bottom | Enhances harmonic richness                |
| Micro-Bubble Effect          | +35 % cavitation efficiency, −12 % sonic threshold | Measured at 2.4 MHz crossover             |
| Output Modes                 | Aggressive ionizing / Gentle restorative | Switchable via head geometry               |

## 6. Safety & Operational Notes
- PTFE liner prevents gallium creep; TiC outer shell contains sonic pressures.  
- Galinstan is contained; DMSO provides viscosity and polarity tuning.  
- High-frequency cavitation may generate localized micro-plasma; eye and ear protection recommended during testing.  
- **Micro-bubbles remain fully contained** — no release of mercury vapor under normal operation.  
- A starburst plasma configuration (spine / cell-membrane analogue) observed at healing-head crossover – significantly intensified by micro-bubble seeding; documented for further plasma-physics study.

**Version 5 considerations:** integrated optical diagnostics, automated sphere-size gradient control, and variable micro-bubble resonance tuning.

